.TH KWYBARS 1 "May 2026" "Kwybars 0.1.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kwybars \- GTK4 Wayland audio visualizer overlay
.br
kwybars-daemon \- start and supervise the Kwybars overlay
.br
kwybars-overlay \- render the visualizer overlay
.br
kwybarsctl \- inspect and manage Kwybars configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kwybars-daemon
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kwybars-overlay
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kwybarsctl
.RI command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Kwybars
is a Wayland-first desktop audio visualizer. It renders GTK4 bars as a transparent layer-shell overlay, usually anchored to a desktop edge.
.PP
The recommended runtime entrypoint is
.BR kwybars-daemon .
The daemon watches audio activity, starts
.B kwybars-overlay
when audio becomes active, stops it after silence when configured to do so, and shares one audio frame stream with the overlay process.
.PP
The
.B kwybars-overlay
binary owns the GTK/layer-shell window and rendering loop. It can be launched directly for development or troubleshooting, but daemon launch is preferred for normal desktop use.
.PP
The
.B kwybarsctl
binary provides read-only diagnostics plus safe config and image-overlay helpers.
.SH DAEMON OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show daemon help.
.TP
.BI -c,\ --config\  PATH
Load a specific configuration file.
.TP
.BI --config= PATH
Load a specific configuration file.
.SH OVERLAY OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show overlay help.
.TP
.BI -c,\ --config\  PATH
Load a specific configuration file.
.TP
.BI --config= PATH
Load a specific configuration file.
.SH CONTROL COMMANDS
.TP
.B switch-config [--active PATH] TARGET
Atomically replace the active config path with a symlink to
.IR TARGET .
By default, the active path is the normal Kwybars config path.
.TP
.B image-overlay match --overlay-dir DIR [--config PATH] WALLPAPER
Match
.I WALLPAPER
by filename stem against images in
.IR DIR ,
then set
.B [image_overlay].enabled
and
.B [image_overlay].path
in the selected config. The lookup order is
.IR png ,
.IR webp ,
.IR jpg ,
then
.IR jpeg .
.TP
.B validate-config [--config PATH]
Validate the selected config file, adjacent
.IR colors.toml ,
and configured theme. A positional config path may be used instead of
.BR --config .
.TP
.B doctor [--config PATH]
Print local runtime diagnostics, including Wayland session detection, Cava availability, config parse status, theme status, selected overlay values, and overlay frame-source state.
.TP
.B list-themes [--config PATH]
List available user, packaged, and source-checkout themes using the same precedence as the runtime.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show control command help.
.SH CONTROL OPTIONS
.TP
.BI -a,\ --active\  PATH
Active config path to update for
.BR switch-config .
.TP
.BI -c,\ --config\  PATH
Config path to update, validate, inspect, or use for theme lookup.
.TP
.BI --overlay-dir\  DIR
Directory containing images for
.B image-overlay match
lookups.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The default config path is resolved in this order:
.IP "1." 4
.B KWYBARS_CONFIG
.IP "2." 4
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kwybars/config.toml
.IP "3." 4
.B $HOME/.config/kwybars/config.toml
.IP "4." 4
.B ./kwybars.toml
.PP
If no config exists, Kwybars uses built-in defaults. Packaged examples are installed under
.BR /usr/share/doc/kwybars/examples/ ,
and source checkouts include examples under
.BR assets/examples/ .
.PP
Adjacent
.B colors.toml
files can override visualizer colors for the active config.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kwybars/config.toml
Default user configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kwybars/colors.toml
Optional adjacent color override file.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kwybars/themes/
User theme directory.
.TP
.I /usr/share/kwybars/themes/
Packaged built-in themes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/kwybars/examples/
Packaged example configurations.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/kwybars-daemon.service
Packaged user service.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kwybars/daemon.log
Default daemon log file when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/kwybars/overlay.log
Default overlay log file when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KWYBARS_CONFIG
Overrides the default config path.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_THEMES_DIR
Overrides the packaged built-in theme directory.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_LOG
Controls tracing verbosity. Falls back to
.B RUST_LOG
when unset.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_LOG_FILE
Overrides the log file target for the current process.
.TP
.B KWYBARS_FRAME_SOCKET
Internal daemon-to-overlay frame stream socket. Normally set by
.BR kwybars-daemon .
.TP
.B KWYBARS_DISABLE_NOTIFICATIONS
Internal flag used to suppress duplicate overlay notifications when launched by the daemon.
.TP
.B GSK_RENDERER
GTK renderer override. The overlay defaults this to
.B cairo
when unset.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland display socket name. Required for overlay display, though the daemon can recover from some missing environment cases by inspecting
.BR XDG_RUNTIME_DIR .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the daemon manually:
.B kwybars-daemon
.TP
Start with an explicit config:
.B kwybars-daemon --config ~/.config/kwybars/config.toml
.TP
Run the overlay directly:
.B kwybars-overlay --config ./assets/examples/wave.toml
.TP
Validate config:
.B kwybarsctl validate-config
.TP
Run diagnostics:
.B kwybarsctl doctor
.TP
List themes:
.B kwybarsctl list-themes
.TP
Switch the active config symlink:
.B kwybarsctl switch-config ~/.config/kwybars/presets/wave.toml
.TP
Match a wallpaper to an image overlay:
.B kwybarsctl image-overlay match --overlay-dir ~/.config/kwybars/wallpaper-overlays ~/Pictures/wallpapers/forest.jpg
.TP
Enable the packaged user service:
.B systemctl --user enable --now kwybars-daemon.service
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cava (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR journalctl (1)
